                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div>
<p><span>The health impact assessment (HIA) serves as a supporting factor for the implementation of the Healthy China 2030 Plan and is one of the cornerstones of the health governance system. Since the 1970s, environmental and social impact assessments have become well-established, widely applied, and have generated many practitioners and professional organizations. However, HIA still lacks a mature institutional framework and suffers from a shortage of implementation capacity. This course systematically introduces the theoretical foundations, development history, methodological tools, and implementation steps of HIA; comprehensively explains how HIA can be embedded into macro-level processes such as policy formulation, cross-sectoral collaboration, and decision-making translation; and presents an overview of HIA institutional development in representative countries along with successful practical cases. The course covers both methodology and policy integration, supplemented by case-based teaching, aiming to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of HIA and practical tools.</span></p>
</div></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
